## 5. Motion rules (no errors on scroll)

- Every reveal is one-shot and independent of `window.load`. Elements already in view when the page mounts are revealed on mount. Navigating away and back re-runs reveals because components remount.
- Timers, observers and listeners are cleaned up on unmount; the typewriter never writes to state after unmount.
- Fast scrolling past an element must still end with it revealed (IntersectionObserver `rootMargin: '0px 0px -10% 0px'`, and also reveal when the element is fully above the viewport).
- The typed bid request area has a fixed height (spec: 250u) so typing never shifts layout.
- Anchor links use `scrollIntoView({ behavior })` with `behavior: 'auto'` under reduced motion, and `scroll-margin-top: 90px` on the anchor sections.

