# PART 4 — BACKEND, FORMS, AUTH, DATA PAGES

## 0. How to read this part

Everything built so far stays unchanged except where this part says so. Follow `docs/ENGINEERING.md`, especially "Failure handling" and "Security". The question to ask about every piece of code here is not "does it work" but "what breaks, and who can abuse it". Work in this order: (a) plan in `docs/plan-4.md`; (b) write `docs/DATA.md` (entities, access rules, functions) and `docs/SECURITY.md` (threats considered and how each is handled, one line each); (c) implement; (d) check section 9 and record pass/fail in `docs/verification-4.md`. If the platform cannot do something this part requires (for example anonymous function calls), say so in `docs/verification-4.md`; never weaken a security rule to make something work.

## 1. Scope

Eight pages become real: `/contact`, `/book-a-call`, `/get-started`, `/opt-out`, `/login`, `/stories`, `/resources/partners`, `/resources/status`. Plus: the entities, backend functions, a form layer, an auth hook, a live status chip in the footer, and a logged-in state in the navigation.

## 2. Data model (platform-managed database)

Use the platform's managed database and entities. One entity per concept. Field names are snake_case. Do not store things you filter or sort on inside nested objects. Filter only on `request_id`, `email`, `created_date`, `is_published`, `category` and `state`. Do not seed any records.

