- A `request_id` (UUID from `crypto.randomUUID()`) is created once when the form mounts and renewed only after a successful submit.
- States: idle, submitting (button disabled and shows the label with "…"; a second click does nothing), success (the form is replaced by a success panel with a button to send another), error (inline message above the button; the fields keep their values).
- The honeypot is a text input named `website`, off-screen (not `display:none`), `tabIndex={-1}`, `autoComplete="off"`, `aria-hidden="true"`.
- A timeout shows the `timeout` message and the user can press send again safely.
- `/contact` reads `?topic=` and preselects the topic only if it is one of the three allowed values.
