## 9. Acceptance criteria (record results in `docs/verification-4.md`)

1. **Access.** As an anonymous visitor, from the browser console, list and create on each of the eight entities are denied. No function returns a submission or a record by id.
2. **Happy path.** Each of the four forms with valid data creates exactly one record with the right fields, shows the success panel, and a reload does not resubmit.
3. **Idempotency.** Double-clicking submit, pressing Enter twice, or retrying after a timeout creates one record.
4. **Hostile input.** An empty body, a body over 10 KB, a 2,001-character message, a wrong enum, an unknown field, `kind` set to something else, a missing consent, and a message containing `<script>alert(1)</script>` are each rejected or stored as inert text and are never rendered as HTML anywhere.
5. **Honeypot.** With the hidden field filled, the UI shows success and no record exists.
6. **Rate limit.** The fourth submission with the same email within 10 minutes is refused with the `rate_limited` message. A failing count query results in `unavailable` and no record (confirm by reading the code path).
7. **Offline and slow.** With the network off, or a slow function, the form shows an error state, keeps its values, and a retry works without duplicates.
8. **Public data.** Unpublished partners, stories and incidents never appear; responses contain only the whitelisted fields; an `http://` website link is not rendered.
9. **Auth.** Login, registration with the verification code, and Google login work; a wrong password shows the generic message; the navigation shows the avatar when signed in and "Гарах" signs out; reloading keeps the state; nothing sensitive is logged to the console.
10. **Footer chip.** Hidden while loading, on error and with no data; shows the right text and links to the status page when data exists.
11. **Responsive.** All eight pages have no horizontal overflow at 360, 390, 768, 820, 821, 1100, 1440 and 1920px; select menus and error text wrap; the form card never exceeds the viewport.
12. **Hygiene.** No secrets in the client bundle or the repo, no packages outside the allowed list in Part 0, no console errors or warnings, no personal data in any log, `docs/DATA.md` and `docs/SECURITY.md` exist and match the code.

## 10. Reminder (highest priority)

